# Cloudflare Pages reads this from the deployed root.

# The blog redirects (/blog, /blog/, /blog/* to /) came out on 2026-11-04 when
# the blog came back. Pages caches responses at its own edge with a 7-day
# s-maxage that the zone purge API cannot reach, and a redirect at a path is the
# one thing found to replace a cached object there; see /dad/ below.

# /dad/ was published for a few hours and is now local only. Same problem as the
# blog above and the same fix: deleting the page left Pages serving a cached
# copy for a week with no way to evict it, so this REPLACES the cached object
# rather than trying to delete it. Without these lines parkerhunt.me/dad/ keeps
# answering 200 while the deployment it came from answers 404.
/dad      /  301
/dad/     /  301
/dad/*    /  301
